  },
  "limitations": [
    "Each non-landslide point shares its paired landslide's date and region (same weather system, within about one IMERG cell), so rainfall is nearly identical within a pair by design; this dataset cannot support a rainfall-amount threshold.",
    "Landslide dates are satellite-image dates of scar-mapping layers, not occurrence dates; ~16 percent may have day and month swapped (docs/METHODS.md, Known issues 3).",
    "ROC-AUC reported here measures whether small within-pair rainfall differences carry any signal -- it is not a measure of how well rainfall alone predicts landslides in the real world.",
    "No real-world-prevalence rainfall sample (e.g. random dates/locations regardless of paired landslide wetness) has been collected; building one is the natural next step for an operationally calibrated rainfall trigger threshold.",
    "Thresholds/metrics here describe relative model ranking, not an operational alert threshold."
  ]
